<title>USA: SSE Telecom gets order from MCI.</title>
<headline>SSE Telecom gets order from MCI.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA, Va. 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>SSE Telecom Inc said on Friday it had received a $500,000 order for satellite earth station equipment to be delivered to MCI Communications Corp for the U.S. Federal Aviation Administration.</p>
<p>SSE is part of the MCI group that recently won the $165 million contract for a satellite communications system for the FAA.</p>
<p>This initial order includes satellite modems, RF subsystems and remote interface controllers for large and small satellite earth station configurations, SSE said.</p>
</text>
